# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# This tree is authored on Windows and tested on ubuntu-latest in CI. Without this, files
# committed from Windows land with CRLF, and the first contributor on macOS or Linux produces
# a diff touching every line of every file they open — which buries the actual change and makes
# `git blame` useless for finding out why a county is assigned the way it is.
#
# Working copies keep whatever their platform prefers; only what git stores is normalized.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The crosswalk is read by humans in diffs. A corrected ZIP should show as one changed line.
*.json text eol=lf
